2 2026. That was the first decline in three years, after +3.1% in Q4 2025 and +1.8% in Q1 2026 (n3.d2, n3.d5).\n- Voltaris shipments fell 9% in Q2, the steepest among large makers (n3.d2).\n- Voltaris's share of Caldrian shipments dropped from 31% to 27%. Tarnwell and imports gained (n3.d3).\n- Shipments typically trail orders by about two quarters (n3.d2). The Q2 decline therefore points to weak orders in late 2025 or early 2026, and shipments in H2 2026 and early 2027 probably stay weak.\n- Quarterly revenue was C$905M, 960M, 980M and 890M for 2025Q3 to 2026Q2. The last four quarters sum to about C$3.74B (n3.d4).\n\n**Estimate**\n- Annualizing Q2 2026 revenue gives about C$3.56B.\n- Annualizing H1 2026 gives about C$3.74B.\n- If the industry is flat to slightly down and Voltaris holds 27% share, 2027 revenue is about C$3.4–3.7B.\n- If share recovers and the industry grows 3%, revenue is about C$3.8B.\n- Reaching C$4.2B would need both a share rebound toward 31% and industry growth. That would be about a 15% rise in shipments from the Q2 level.\n- Pricing could add some upside. I have no price data here, so this is not in the range.\n\n**Caveat:** The data ends at Q2 2026. Orders and backlog, which n2 is covering, could change this view.","ttft_ms":1833,"type":"result","duration_ms":16067,"uuid":"402216f2-80a1-4af5-8679-992370badbb8","ttft_stream_ms":1120,"time_to_request_ms":56,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":6,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":59,"time_to